      "text": "To find the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\), we need to first determine the coefficients \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) for the polynomial \\(f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\). From the graph, we can see that the polynomial has roots at \\(x = -2\\), \\(x = -1\\), and \\(x = 1\\). Therefore, we can write the polynomial as:\n\n\\[ f(x) = a(x + 2)(x + 1)(x - 1) \\]\n\nFirst, we need to expand the expression \\((x + 2)(x + 1)(x - 1)\\):\n\n\\[ (x + 2)(x + 1)(x - 1) = (x + 2)(x^2 - 1) = x^3 + 2x^2 - x - 2 \\]\n\nNow, we multiply this result by \\(a\\) to get the polynomial \\(f(x)\\):\n\n\\[ f(x) = a(x^3 + 2x^2 - x - 2) = ax^3 + 2ax^2 - ax - 2a \\]\n\nFrom this, we can identify the coefficients:\n- \\(a = a\\)\n- \\(b = 2a\\)\n- \\(c = -a\\)\n- \\(d = -2a\\)\n\nNow, we want to find the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\). Substituting the values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\), we get:\n\n\\[ 8a - 4b + 2c - d = 8a - 4(2a) + 2(-a) - (-2a) \\]\n\\[ = 8a - 8a - 2a + 2a \\]\n\\[ = -2a \\]\n\nSince doubling both sides does not change the equation:\n\\[ 2a = -2a \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-2a}\n\\]",
